# Cursor / AI agent rules — design-first Astro + SST project
#
# Full version lives in CLAUDE.md. Summary of the non-negotiable workflow:

## Components
- Storybook is the component inventory. Before building a component, check
  `src/components/ui/` and Storybook (http://localhost:6006). Reuse before you
  create — never make a duplicate component.
- Write `Component.stories.tsx` BEFORE `Component.tsx`. Stories define the prop
  API and every visual state (default, loading, error, empty).
- Keep `Component.stories.tsx` next to `Component.tsx`.
- Pages and island containers only ASSEMBLE existing stories; they must not
  invent new visual states inline.

## API
- `src/api/openapi.yaml` is the API contract. Edit the spec BEFORE the handler.
- After editing the spec, run `npm run api:types` to regenerate
  `src/api/schema.gen.ts`. Never edit that file by hand.
- Handlers import the generated `paths` types and cannot return a shape the
  spec doesn't describe. Need a new shape? Change the spec first.
- Wire the route in `sst.config.ts` alongside the handler.

## Verify before done
- `npm run api:types && npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`
- `npm run build`
- `npm test`
